    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Climate change mitigation pathways",
    "problem": "Policymakers lack robust information on emission pathways consistent with the 2\u00b0C temperature limit because this requires integrating the socio-economic feasibility of emission reductions with the uncertain physical processes that link emissions to global temperature rise.",
    "method": "The authors reanalyse a large set of published emission scenarios from integrated assessment models using a risk-based climate modelling framework to identify the characteristics of pathways consistent with limiting global average temperature increase to below 2\u00b0C.",
    "task": "The task is to determine the characteristics of future greenhouse-gas emission pathways consistent with limiting global temperature increase to below 2\u00b0C by reanalysing a large set of published scenarios from integrated assessment models within a risk-based climate modelling framework.",
